OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786234686
OL,3,CTemperatures to rise on Sunday as UK
OL,4,Cbraces for fifth heatwave
OL,6,FWith another heatwave on the way,
OL,7,Fhealth officials have warned of risks
OL,8,Fwhen taking some medicines, including
OL,9,Fibuprofen, in hot weather as they can
OL,10,Fmake it harder for the body to stay
OL,11,Fhydrated, regulate temperature or cope
OL,12,Fwith sun exposure.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30204
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786234686
OL,3,CTemperatures to rise on Sunday as UK
OL,4,Cbraces for fifth heatwave
OL,6,FDr Alison Cave, chief safety officer
OL,7,Fat the Medicines and Healthcare
OL,8,Fproducts Regulatory Agency, said:
OL,9,F"Proton pump inhibitors (PPIs),
OL,10,Fcommonly used to treat acid reflux and
OL,11,Fheartburn, have also been linked to a
OL,12,Fvery low risk of a lupus-like skin
OL,13,Freaction triggered by sun exposure,
OL,14,Fand common painkillers such as
OL,15,Fibuprofen and naproxen may also
OL,16,Fincrease sun sensitivity."
OL,26,@qD@AOUxD@ZO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/11
