OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786234686
OL,3,CTemperatures to rise on Sunday as UK
OL,4,Cbraces for fifth heatwave
OL,6,FReservoir storage in England has
OL,7,Fdropped to 69%, down from 72% a week
OL,8,Fago and nearly 12 percentage points
OL,9,Fbelow the long-term average for the
OL,10,Ftime of year, the Environment Agency
OL,11,Fsaid on Friday.
OL,13,FStorage stood at 85% at the end of
OL,14,FJune, which was the average for that
OL,15,Fpoint in the year, but has fallen
OL,16,Fsteadily in recent weeks.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30210
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786234686
OL,3,CTemperatures to rise on Sunday as UK
OL,4,Cbraces for fifth heatwave
OL,6,FFive reservoirs are now classed as
OL,7,Fhaving "exceptionally low" levels:
OL,8,FBlagdon in Somerset (54% full);
OL,9,FClywedog in Powys, which provides
OL,10,Fwater for central and north-west
OL,11,FEngland (62%); the Dove group of
OL,12,Freservoirs in Derbyshire (74%);
OL,13,FHanningfield in Essex (60%); and
OL,14,FWimbleball in Somerset (50%).
OL,16,FLast month was the driest July for
OL,17,FEngland and Wales since records began
OL,18,Fin 1836, according to provisional
OL,19,Ffigures released by the Met Office.
OL,26,@oD@HOUoD@ZO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/11
